🚽 Issue #282, the exact reproduction: a giga (long) value above 2^32 used to
🚽 truncate (5000000000 printed 705032704) because storage, the atoi literal
🚽 path, and native-call marshalling were all 32-bit. giga now round-trips the
🚽 full value. (This is about value width; sizeof(giga) reporting 4 on wasm32
🚽 is the separate, still-open #177 -- not exercised here.)
skibidi main {
    giga rizz x = 5000000000;
    yapping("%lld", x);          🚽 5000000000, not 705032704

    giga rizz y = x * 2;
    yapping("%lld", y);          🚽 10000000000

    bussin 0;
}
